# novadeck INSTALLER /etc/os-release (Phase 6).
#
# Installed as /etc/os-release by install/mkroot.sh, the way images/os-release is installed by
# images/customize-base.sh — see that file for why a from-packages bootstrap has to own this
# rather than inherit the vendor's.
#
# WHY A SECOND FILE RATHER THAN REUSING images/os-release. The two images are not the same
# product and the difference has to be legible from inside a running system. `ID=novadeck` is what
# the shipped image answers, and the install spine's own rules key off "is this disk ours" — so an
# installer that also answered `novadeck` would be a device claiming to be an install of the thing
# it is about to install. It is also the string a person reads off a fallback console at the moment
# something has gone wrong (novadeck-installer-console.service), where "which image am I even
# looking at" is the first question.
#
# NO PER-BUILD FIELDS HERE, same rule as the main image: this file is static so a rebuild does not
# churn the tree. install/mkroot.sh appends VERSION/VERSION_ID/BUILD_ID for the build it is making.
#
# ID_LIKE lists novadeck first and arch second: tooling that branches on "is this a novadeck
# system" should match, and tooling that branches on distro family gets the Arch answer that this
# actually is.
NAME="NovaDeck Installer"
PRETTY_NAME="NovaDeck Installer"
ID=novadeck-installer
ID_LIKE="novadeck arch"
ANSI_COLOR="1;35"
HOME_URL="https://github.com/Nova-Deck/os-build"
